WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.229 --> 00:00:05.730
Let's talk a little bit about the trajectory,
the future trajectory of the White House Coronavirus

00:00:05.730 --> 00:00:06.730
Taskforce.

00:00:06.730 --> 00:00:11.469
The news is that Donald Trump is now thinking
of canceling the White House coronavirus task

00:00:11.469 --> 00:00:20.140
force even as deaths again spiked yesterday
to 20 350 in a single day.

00:00:20.140 --> 00:00:25.320
And this is this is like much of what Trump
has done in the last two months when it comes

00:00:25.320 --> 00:00:28.939
to coronavirus, which is just a bad bone headed
idea.

00:00:28.939 --> 00:00:34.770
But if your concern is just propaganda and
pretending that you're doing a good job instead

00:00:34.770 --> 00:00:40.000
of dealing with the virus, this is exactly
what we would expect Donald Trump to do.

00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:41.000
The task force.

00:00:41.000 --> 00:00:43.520
I'll remind you, was formed at the end of
January.

00:00:43.520 --> 00:00:48.420
This is the task force where Mike Pence's,
I guess the official head of the task force,

00:00:48.420 --> 00:00:51.870
Dr. Deborah Birks, is the response coordinator.

00:00:51.870 --> 00:00:54.100
You've got the surgeon general on the task
force.

00:00:54.100 --> 00:00:57.640
You have that secretary of Health and Human
Services, Alex Azar, on it.

00:00:57.640 --> 00:01:03.040
He's the one who initially put a former dog
breeder of Labradoodles in charge of the day

00:01:03.040 --> 00:01:04.040
to day.

00:01:04.040 --> 00:01:05.400
Dr. she's on the task force.

00:01:05.400 --> 00:01:09.290
The commissioner of the FDA, Steven Hahn,
is on it.

00:01:09.290 --> 00:01:12.380
Ben Carson is not just a whole bunch of people
on this task force.

00:01:12.380 --> 00:01:19.820
Now, as it is, the task force has not been
super concerned with health and has been too

00:01:19.820 --> 00:01:21.330
concerned with politics.

00:01:21.330 --> 00:01:26.350
Towards the end of the press briefings, we
would see Dr. Burke's become more a vector

00:01:26.350 --> 00:01:28.550
of disinformation than of science.

00:01:28.550 --> 00:01:30.320
And that was a horrible thing.

00:01:30.320 --> 00:01:35.240
But at least you had a task force that was
briefing us daily while the press briefings

00:01:35.240 --> 00:01:38.950
went horribly wrong after the bleach injection
fiasco.

00:01:38.950 --> 00:01:42.740
We've seen those be pared down, really stopped
at this point.

00:01:42.740 --> 00:01:45.830
We no longer see Dr. Fouchier, Dr. Burke's
daily.

00:01:45.830 --> 00:01:48.210
Other than in corporate media interviews.

00:01:48.210 --> 00:01:53.270
And instead, Donald Trump has replaced the
Corona virus press briefings with these economic.

00:01:53.270 --> 00:01:59.320
I guess I'd call them economic agitprop events
with business CEOs and other brown nosing

00:01:59.320 --> 00:02:00.320
sycophants.

00:02:00.320 --> 00:02:01.390
But the cases aren't going down.

00:02:01.390 --> 00:02:06.600
So if you are prioritizing paying attention
to the data rather than whether Trump praises

00:02:06.600 --> 00:02:13.700
CEOs, we are still finding about 25000 new
coronavirus cases basically every single day,

00:02:13.700 --> 00:02:15.709
sometimes more, sometimes a little less.

00:02:15.709 --> 00:02:22.640
And deaths, again, have spiked yesterday,
20, 350 deaths in one day in the United States.

00:02:22.640 --> 00:02:24.190
A really bad number.

00:02:24.190 --> 00:02:28.459
And when you look at what's going on in Italy,
when you look at what's going on in Spain,

00:02:28.459 --> 00:02:32.840
when you look at the curves and then you see
what's going on here, it's not good.

00:02:32.840 --> 00:02:39.069
And meanwhile, as I told you yesterday, CDC
and FEMA have a report which says they fear

00:02:39.069 --> 00:02:46.709
that deaths might actually climb to 3000 a
day by June 1st with maybe 200000 new cases

00:02:46.709 --> 00:02:47.709
a day.

00:02:47.709 --> 00:02:48.709
Now, I hope that doesn't happen.

00:02:48.709 --> 00:02:52.299
As you all know, politics don't play a role
in what I hope happens.

00:02:52.299 --> 00:02:57.890
I don't hope we have one single death for
the purpose of making Trump look bad or helping

00:02:57.890 --> 00:02:58.890
to defeat Trump.

00:02:58.890 --> 00:03:01.150
The case for that is very clear.

00:03:01.150 --> 00:03:02.319
There have been enough deaths.

00:03:02.319 --> 00:03:04.079
I don't want anyone to die.

00:03:04.079 --> 00:03:05.799
Hopefully it won't happen.

00:03:05.799 --> 00:03:09.280
But the numbers in a lot of states aren't
looking good.

00:03:09.280 --> 00:03:10.349
Here's Donald Trump.

00:03:10.349 --> 00:03:16.379
Asked yesterday in Arizona about the Corona
virus task force, Trump stopped at a Honeywell

00:03:16.379 --> 00:03:18.129
mask required factory.

00:03:18.129 --> 00:03:19.370
He refused to wear a mask.

00:03:19.370 --> 00:03:21.050
I'll talk about that later.

00:03:21.050 --> 00:03:25.829
But Donald Trump again talking about we've
just done great about everything.

00:03:25.829 --> 00:03:30.749
And at one point, he Trump walked around all
day yesterday with a piece of paper in his

00:03:30.749 --> 00:03:31.749
pocket.

00:03:31.749 --> 00:03:36.510
That was just a graph of the total number
of coronavirus tests, which is meaningless.

00:03:36.510 --> 00:03:37.510
Right.

00:03:37.510 --> 00:03:38.799
We've talked about per capita.

00:03:38.799 --> 00:03:39.830
Here is Donald Trump's answer.

00:03:39.830 --> 00:03:42.520
And it includes pulling out that piece of
paper.

00:03:42.520 --> 00:03:48.590
When asked about why would you now disband
the Corona virus task force, saying, don't

00:03:48.590 --> 00:03:53.739
you want me to say that we've done an incredible
job on testing?

00:03:53.739 --> 00:03:58.700
With that being said, we have some additional
important antibody tests coming up that will

00:03:58.700 --> 00:04:00.060
even blow these numbers away.

00:04:00.060 --> 00:04:02.139
But nobody's done the job we're doing.

00:04:02.139 --> 00:04:08.230
You need to continue to meet with the task
force to get this scientific expertise.

00:04:08.230 --> 00:04:13.419
We will certain people as an example.

00:04:13.419 --> 00:04:14.780
We have hospitals that we built.

00:04:14.780 --> 00:04:16.730
We have medical centers that we built.

00:04:16.730 --> 00:04:19.380
We have people on the taskforce that focus
on that.

00:04:19.380 --> 00:04:21.170
We have people on the task force.

00:04:21.170 --> 00:04:23.250
Focused exclusively on ventilators.

00:04:23.250 --> 00:04:27.830
Well, we have more ventilators now than anybody
in the world, and we're helping France, as

00:04:27.830 --> 00:04:31.360
you know, we're helping France, Italy, Spain,
Nigeria.

00:04:31.360 --> 00:04:35.320
We're just we're giving, I think, 250 in Nigeria.

00:04:35.320 --> 00:04:37.240
We have many countries that we're helping.

00:04:37.240 --> 00:04:38.710
But the ventilator problem itself.

00:04:38.710 --> 00:04:40.190
So you don't need that.

00:04:40.190 --> 00:04:45.610
We have now a different sort of a combination
of safety and reopening.

00:04:45.610 --> 00:04:47.900
So we'll have something in a different form.

00:04:47.900 --> 00:04:53.770
But the task force for what we've done, I
think everybody out there, when they're being

00:04:53.770 --> 00:04:59.390
very honest, I think the job we've done on
testing will shortly be and maybe even supersede

00:04:59.390 --> 00:05:04.470
the job that we've done on the ventilators,
which people can't even believe we had to

00:05:04.470 --> 00:05:06.110
call the other day when the governors.

00:05:06.110 --> 00:05:08.490
So it goes on for about an additional minute.

00:05:08.490 --> 00:05:10.240
But as you can tell, there's no answer.

00:05:10.240 --> 00:05:11.240
There's no answer.

00:05:11.240 --> 00:05:14.410
The question was, should you really end the
coronavirus task force?

00:05:14.410 --> 00:05:18.990
When we are in the middle of a pandemic and
Trump says governors are happy, we have tons

00:05:18.990 --> 00:05:23.040
of ventilators and I have a piece of paper
with a graph about testing.

00:05:23.040 --> 00:05:27.580
It's striking me as counter intuitive to end
the task force now.

00:05:27.580 --> 00:05:29.970
And I want to point out one other thing.

00:05:29.970 --> 00:05:34.140
We've been watching the numbers coming out
of some of these early openings, southern

00:05:34.140 --> 00:05:35.140
states.

00:05:35.140 --> 00:05:39.330
The states that didn't have these are states
that weren't initially hot spots and they

00:05:39.330 --> 00:05:42.490
insisted that they're good to go and reopen.

00:05:42.490 --> 00:05:43.820
The numbers aren't good.

00:05:43.820 --> 00:05:46.040
Look at just one example out of Texas.

00:05:46.040 --> 00:05:51.240
In Texas, cases have increased dramatically
over the last nine days.

00:05:51.240 --> 00:05:59.580
Texas had 535 new cases on April 27 that went
up to 960 new cases on April 30.

00:05:59.580 --> 00:06:02.870
And that was up to more than 12 hundred new
cases yesterday.

00:06:02.870 --> 00:06:07.700
Now, understand, the raw numbers are not the
important thing here.

00:06:07.700 --> 00:06:13.650
The percentage increases are if you see new
cases continue to increase in Texas at this

00:06:13.650 --> 00:06:14.660
rate.

00:06:14.660 --> 00:06:20.600
There are 34000 cases will be more than 50000
cases just 10 days from now.

00:06:20.600 --> 00:06:26.960
And by then, if the other North-Eastern and
West Coast states keep seeing declines, Texas

00:06:26.960 --> 00:06:31.320
will have dramatically more active cases than
any of these early hotspots.

00:06:31.320 --> 00:06:34.220
We can do a similar analysis in other states.

00:06:34.220 --> 00:06:36.270
I hope none of this happens.

00:06:36.270 --> 00:06:41.240
But the last thing you need right now is to
end the task force and just focus on reopening

00:06:41.240 --> 00:06:45.770
since it's that reopening which may indeed
wreak havoc in a whole bunch of states.

00:06:45.770 --> 00:06:47.070
Hope it doesn't happen.

00:06:47.070 --> 00:08:09.270
What the data is pointing to.

